# Story 34: Cloud Sharing (55s)
# Hook: Share your panes to the cloud -- view mode or full control.
# Duration: 55s
# Source: story-34-cloud-sharing.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 10

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- your collaborative terminal.

[00:04.0 --> 00:08.0]
We will share this pane to the cloud.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
##share pane view creates a read-only cloud link. Remote users can watch but not type.

[00:14.0 --> 00:20.0]
##share list shows all active shares with their IDs.

[00:20.0 --> 00:26.0]
##unshare pane revokes the cloud link.

[00:26.0 --> 00:32.0]
##share pane control allows remote users to type commands. Use this for pair programming or remote assistance.

[00:32.0 --> 00:38.0]
The share list now shows the control share.

[00:38.0 --> 00:44.0]
Revoke the control share when done.

[00:44.0 --> 00:48.0]
All shares removed -- your terminal is private again.

[00:48.0 --> 00:55.0]
Cloud sharing -- view or control, instantly shareable.

